.DS_Store
proxmox-automated-install/
.continue/
**/data/*
!**/data/.gitkeep

# CIAB framework catalogs (CIS IG1, NIST CSF, etc.) — version-controlled reference data.
!**/data/frameworks/
!**/data/frameworks/**

# CIAB threat scenario library — canonical starter findings, version-controlled.
!**/data/threat-scenario-library.json

# CIAB GOAD role manifest — the vendored, pinned description of upstream GOAD's
# ansible role library. This one MUST stay tracked: GOAD-main/ is ignored below
# and has no tracked files, so this manifest is the only reviewable record of
# what the baked controller actually runs. Ignoring it would recreate exactly
# the invisibility it exists to fix (see ciab/utils/goad-role-manifest.js).
!**/data/goad-role-manifest.json

# CIAB GOAD corpus calibration baseline — the written verdict for every finding
# the validator emits against the eight shipped upstream labs, with the file:line
# evidence and the runtime consequence for each. ciab-goad-lab-validate.test.js
# asserts the pinned finding set against this document, so an ignored copy is an
# artifact that exists only on the authoring machine and shows up in no diff —
# the same failure the manifest negation above exists to prevent.
!**/data/goad-corpus-findings.md

# CIAB GOAD post-condition probe — the read-only PowerShell that asserts what is
# ACTUALLY TRUE in a baked lab (see ciab/utils/goad-postcondition-probe.js). It is
# staged to a guest at run time, so it is data rather than a module this process
# requires, but it is the executable half of the contract with the parser and has to
# be reviewable in a diff. BOTH lines are required — `**/data/*` on line 4 excludes
# the probe DIRECTORY itself and git never descends into an excluded directory, so
# the /** negation alone would re-include nothing (same pairing, same reason, as the
# frameworks/ and chassis/ rules).
!**/data/probe/
!**/data/probe/**

# CIAB GOAD chassis — the three stripped lab skeletons (S/M/L) the AD compiler
# repopulates per client profile. COMPILE-TIME INPUT, not a runtime artifact:
# the compiler reads these on the orchestrator and emits ad/CIAB-<hash>/, which
# is pushed to the controller separately — the controller never reads a chassis.
# They live here rather than in GOAD-main/ for the same reason the manifest above
# does: GOAD-main/ has zero tracked files, so a chassis kept there would be
# invisible to `node --test` and to every reviewer. BOTH lines are required —
# `**/data/*` on line 4 excludes the chassis DIRECTORY itself, and git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so the /** negation alone would re-include
# nothing (same pairing, same reason, as the frameworks/ rules above).
!**/data/chassis/
!**/data/chassis/**
